{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XGQpfdLzMf8bChEDyDjYZj","type":"tool_result","content":"With `require_approval: true` (the Phase 1 default) the gate posts one \"ready for approval\" comment per lead job and waits. `ard:approved` is honoured only when its latest `labeled` event (reset by an `unlabeled`) is by a collaborator with triage permission or higher, is not the App, and comes after the last triage `:done` label of the issue. An approval given earlier is left in place and ignored: the gate waits for a fresh one and does not escalate. An approval from anyone else adds `ard:needs-human` with a comment that does not name the actor. A human who adds `ard:worker:<role>` directly bypasses the gate and has approved by doing so. The gate does not enforce that `triage:engineer` ran: the lead routes and the gate applies its routing. In `--dry-run` the gate logs `triage.would_gate` and writes nothing; otherwise each action records a `gate` event.\ninternal/triage/candidates.go:41:\t\t// plan.md under it.\ninternal/triage/doc.go:1:// Package triage is the triage loop (#29): it turns an issue into plan.md, one\ninternal/triage/fanin.go:419:\ttext := fmt.Sprintf(\"**ard · triage · ready for approval**\\n\\nTriage is complete; the plan is in `.ard/%d/plan.md`. A maintainer adds `%s` to start the `%s` worker. \"+","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16ee025c-fa9f-459a-ab5e-88271e950e26","uuid":"18be2a71-08a7-4834-9c80-fcaa4a8bc1fb","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:40:38.927Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"With `require_approval: true` (the Phase 1 default) the gate posts one \"ready for approval\" comment per lead job and waits. `ard:approved` is honoured only when its latest `labeled` event (reset by an `unlabeled`) is by a collaborator with triage permission or higher, is not the App, and comes after the last triage `:done` label of the issue. An approval given earlier is left in place and ignored: the gate waits for a fresh one and does not escalate. An approval from anyone else adds `ard:needs-human` with a comment that does not name the actor. A human who adds `ard:worker:<role>` directly bypasses the gate and has approved by doing so. The gate does not enforce that `triage:engineer` ran: the lead routes and the gate applies its routing. In `--dry-run` the gate logs `triage.would_gate` and writes nothing; otherwise each action records a `gate` event.\ninternal/triage/candidates.go:41:\t\t// plan.md under it.\ninternal/triage/doc.go:1:// Package triage is the triage loop (#29): it turns an issue into plan.md, one\ninternal/triage/fanin.go:419:\ttext := fmt.Sprintf(\"**ard · triage · ready for approval**\\n\\nTriage is complete; the plan is in `.ard/%d/plan.md`. A maintainer adds `%s` to start the `%s` worker. \"+","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XGQpfdLzMf8bChEDyDjYZj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
