{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AauFKFMcLTLHPgw8dBSqJ5","type":"tool_result","content":"\t}\n\tif err := setGCOff(ctx, g, tmp); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\treturn os.Rename(tmp, p)\n}\n\n// seedClone fetches main once with a long bound: the first full fetch would\n// otherwise run under the config load's 2 minute limit and could never finish\n// on a large repo. A failure is logged, not returned: serve starts paused (the\n// config load fails the same way) and the next start retries.\nfunc seedClone(ctx context.Context, g cloneGit, p, remoteURL string, token gitx.TokenFunc, log *slog.Logger) {\n\tstart := time.Now()\n\tsctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, seedTimeout)\n\tdefer cancel()\n\tif err := g.FetchRef(sctx, p, remoteURL, \"+refs/heads/main:\"+seedRef, token); err != nil {\n\t\tif ctx.Err() == nil {\n\t\t\tlog.Error(\"serve.clone_seed_failed\", \"error\", err,\n\t\t\t\t\"hint\", \"config loads keep fetching; the next start retries the seed\")\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tsha, _ := g.RevParse(sctx, p, seedRef)\n\tlog.Info(\"serve.clone_seeded\", \"sha\", sha, \"elapsed\", time.Since(start).Round(time.Millisecond))\n}\n\n// removeLegacyLanes deletes the committer-* directories the checkout-based\n// layout kept directly under ~/.ard/work/<owner>/<repo>. No git runs: their\n// registrations in the operator's checkout dangle until the operator prunes.\nfunc removeLegacyLanes(home string, r github.Repo, log *slog.Logger) {\n\tdir, err := repoWorkDir(home, r)\n// Closer, committer or executor. It returns nil, and logs, when the executor\n// cannot be built.\nfunc workerLoop(w *wiring) controller.Loop {\n\tex, err := w.newExecutor()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tw.Log.Error(\"worker.unavailable\", \"error\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tfin, err := w.finisher()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tw.Log.Error(\"worker.unavailable\", \"error\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\treg, err := agent.NewRegistry(claude.New(claude.Options{}))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err) // a duplicate adapter name is a programming error\n\t}\n\treturn worker.New(worker.Deps{\n\t\tReader: w.Reader, Effects: w.Effects, Store: w.Store,\n\t\tExecutor: ex, Finisher: fin, Code: w.branchCommitter(), Git: gitx.New(\"\"),\n\t\tPool:   func() worker.Offerer { return w.Pool() },\n\t\tAgents: reg, Parse: w.parseFunc(), Model: w.Model,\n\t\tSecrets: func() *redact.Secrets { return redact.FromEnviron(os.Environ()) }, HostPaths: w.hostPaths(),\n\t\tRepo: w.Repo, RepoDir: w.Root, RemoteURL: w.RemoteURL, Token: w.Token, Log: w.Log,\n\t})\n}\n   only to override a review that is still `:changes`.) Stop `serve` with Ctrl-C (SIGINT); it stops cleanly\n   between jobs.\n\n**Moving faster than the poll.** Each loop ticks once at startup, then every\ninterval (triage 15 min, workers and reviewers 5 min). To act now, send\n`SIGUSR1` to `serve` (`kill -USR1 <pid of ard serve>`): every loop runs one tick\nimmediately, still behind the kill switch and the job pool, and logs\n`controller.wake`. No restart is needed.\n`ard:approved` counts as soon as triage has finished, so there is no need to\nwait for the \"ready for approval\" comment.\n\n\n   `serve` creates its bare clone under `~/.ard/repos/` on first start.\n5. **Watch.** Expected sequence on the issue:\n   - `ard:triage:lead:running`, then a commit to `main` under `.ard/<n>/`\n     and a close-out comment; `ard:pending` is removed\n   - `ard:triage:engineer` → `:running` → `:done`; `plan.md` gains the\n     engineer's section\n   - a \"ready for approval\" comment. **Read `.ard/<n>/plan.md`**, then add\n     `ard:approved` yourself (it counts only from a human with triage\n     permission, added after triage finished)\n   - `ard:worker:engineer:running`, a `worker/<n>-…` branch and a draft PR\n   - `ard:review:eng-review` on the PR, then a PR review and\n     `ard:review:eng-review:done` or `:changes`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16ee025c-fa9f-459a-ab5e